# Python + Playwright migration
+
+This repository now includes a Python-native execution path alongside the original TypeScript implementation.
+
+Quick start:
+
+```bash
+python -m venv .venv
+source .venv/bin/activate
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+python -m playwright install
+python runner.py --app orangehrm --file VerifyBuzzPostVerification.txt
+```
+
+Available commands:
+
+```bash
+python runner.py --list-apps
+python runner.py --app orangehrm --suite smoke
+python runner.py --app orangehrm --browser firefox --headed
+```
+
+The Python runner reads the same `config/app-configs/*.json` files and the existing prompt files in `prompts/`, so the migration preserves the framework behavior while moving execution to Python + Playwright.
+
